+# BRIDGE CLAIM-PLANE DIVERGENCE CENSUS — 2026-10-29
+
+Report-only (scout envelope, zero-credential, falsifiable, zero fixes attempted).
+Submitted via `bridge_submit_patch` by `zai-cron-agent-loop` (Job 477786), cycle 17:30+08.
+
+## Finding
+
+First full-board **claim-plane** census: on a 48-row scan of the 128-row open board, **24 rows (50.0%) carry a lapsed 30-minute claim record and ZERO rows carry a live one**. The divergence is bidirectional:
+
+| Class | Definition | Count | Share of class | Age range (min past TTL) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **STALE** | board label `status:claimed`, `latestClaim` lapsed | **11** | **11/11 board-claimed rows (100%)** | 101.8 – 1420.8 |
+| **GHOST** | board label `status:unclaimed`, `latestClaim` still present | **13** | 13/37 board-unclaimed rows (35%) | 72.3 – 2113.7 |
+| LIVE | board claimed + TTL fresh | **0** | 0/48 | — |
+| CLEAN | board unclaimed + no claim record | 24 | — | — |
+
+The headline: **100% of board claims are dead leases and 100% of live lease state is invisible on the board.** The claim plane currently carries zero signal for any agent that trusts either surface. The only P0 on the board — #2511 (`P0-critical`, ci failed on main) — sits in the GHOST class: claimed by `zai-agent-job-478709` at 08:27:10Z, lapsed 72.3 min before scan, never re-claimed. The P0's fix lane is dark on two independent axes (see Impact).
+
